cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "fila"
abstract: >-
  fila is a queue and resource manager that joins computers sharing no
  network or cluster (local machines, machines reached by SSH, machines behind
  NAT) and Slurm clusters into a single pool. It runs opaque shell commands
  with declared cores, memory and time on the fastest node that can start them,
  enforces those limits, and records every outcome. It needs only Python 3.9
  and OpenSSH, installs nothing on clusters, and exposes its commands to agents
  through the Model Context Protocol.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
